  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Slovenia 2024 &#x2013; Team leader</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed DRRS Team will act as technical sparring partners for the Post-Flood and Landslide Reconstruction Office in technical (online) expert meetings. The Slovenian counterpart is in the lead to determine the topic and the timeline for the collaboration.Phase 1 &#x2013; Information Sharing (January - February 2024)- Exchange of documentation on constructive flood risk reduction measures, standards, guidebooks, maintenance standards and procedures related to water infrastructure.Phase 2 &#x2013; Organizing digital expert meetings per topic (February/March 2024)- The Slovenian counterpart selected a number of thematic areas where they would like learn more about. Two expert meetings already took place in the preliminary meetings during Q4 2023. It is expected that the next (3) thematic expert meetings will take place in February/March 2024 and will focus on disaster management, communication, and participatory water management.Phase 3 &#x2013; study visit to the Netherlands (TBC) (April 2024)- After the thematic learning and exchanging sessions we&#x2019;ll organize a study visit to the Netherlands to go into the technicalities of what we have discussed during the expert meetings. The proposal is to link the Slovenian counterpart to the Dutch waterboards (e.g. Limburg) and organize a collaborative exchange of experiences and lessons learned.Phase 4 &#x2013; evaluating the collaboration (April 2024 - May 2024)- The Team leader is asked to set up an evaluation call with the Post Flood and Landslide Reconstruction office to determine whether the advice has led to concrete change in policies/ regulatory frameworks/ communication flows etc.</narrative>
  </description>
